{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486709-storypath-patch-for-cod-2e","id":1486709,"title":"Storypath Patch for CoD 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-16T19:01:00-07:00","id":1486709,"title":"Storypath Patch for CoD 2E?","content":"After watching <b>Stranger Things</b> S04, I wondering over doing <b>CoD</b> mortal one-shot. However, for last 2 years I run <b><i>Storypath</i></b> based <b>Scion</b> 2E - and doing preparations <b>Trinity </b>2E and <b>They Came</b> games, also on <i><b>Storypath</b></i>. So I'm much more versed in <i><b>Storypath</b></i> than <i><b>Storytelling</b></i> ( <b>CoD</b>) rules engine, right now.<br /> <br /> In short, I wonder - <b>How much can be transplanted from Storypath to CoD</b> 2E games, without large games overhaul?<br /> <br /> On first glance, I think:<br /> 1. Ideas of <b>Difficulties</b>, <b>Enhancements</b> and <b>Complications</b> to rolls. In <b>CoD</b>, Weapons Damage as Enhancement should notably simplified and make combat much deadlier. \ud83d\ude08<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Splats and Organisations as Paths</b> - Invoking and Revoking of Paths/Splats access could be much fun than in <b>CoD</b> basic. Think how <b><i>Invictus</i> Path</b> can help you get out of trouble in <b>VtR</b> in <b><i>Invoking</i></b> it - but how much trouble you will be with them if they <b><i>Revoked</i></b> you all sweet deals like those. \ud83d\ude2e Or could you get Revoked Inner (X) Splat - like vampires Clan, werewolves Auspice or mages Path-Path? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> 3. Maybe idea of <b>Momentum</b> and <b>Tension</b> to add to <b>CoD</b>? \ud83e\udd14 Its last one I have the most uncertain what would it do to basic <b>CoD</b> game. It surely would go over steps of Willpower points and <b>Virtue &amp; Vice</b> system in <b>CoD</b> - but I for years had problem with <b>V&amp;V</b> as constant generator of Willpower in original <b>nWoD</b> 1E and <b>CoD</b> 2E... Doing '<b>Virtue &amp; Vice </b>as<b> Momentum</b> generation' for whole table seems much more dynamic and fun in play. <br /> <br /> P. S. In <b>Storypath</b> we already have <b>Merits</b>-like mechanics in for of <b>Edges</b>. <b>Trinity </b>from start have Edges, <b>Scion</b> got them as alternative rules in <b>Saints &amp; Monsters</b> book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2022, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T21:00:50-07:00","id":1486714,"title":"","content":"<i>Without a large overhaul?</i><br /> <br /> You've got one system designed to judge each roll granularly, with a budget of successes distributed across a moving target difficulty, complications, and whatever stunts are needed to be effective. You've got another system designed to involve as little granularity as possible, where difficulty is modeled almost entirely by dice modifiers, and the vast majority of rolls outside of combat only effectively care about whether you rolled any successes at all or none. Mage: the Awakening Second Edition, in fact, had to completely overhaul its spellcasting system to properly fit this model.<br /> <br /> You're looking at either a recipe for tons of weird and unexpected probability outcomes and thus play experiences as you mash rolls from one system into the model of the other, or a lot of tedious work converting bespoke roll results tables from one system to fit the other.<br /> <br /> Individual systems could be much more easily translated: if you just kept to a matter of adopting Paths to CofD mechanics, or fusing Willpower into the Momentum and Tension system, those could be done. Paths are probably actually pretty straightforward. Momentum might have some rougher edges due to the differences between the systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 07-17-2022, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:11:46-07:00","id":1486725,"title":"","content":"What is Tension? I don't think I've heard of it...<br /> <br /> Anyways, I feel that WoD translates better to Storypath than CofD, at least for now. Storypath has this action-hero feel that fits better with the sometimes-gonzo dark punk feel that WoD invokes every now and then, despite WoD 5th Edition's more down-to-earth atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Now Paths, I feel would work... maybe call them Tracks to both avoid an obvious name-clashing issue, and emphasize how in the CofD the world sometimes dunks you straight to the gutters without much of your input. (To me the word 'path' feels more self-determinable, while 'track' feels less so) (We already have Aspirations as things that the player can want to happen to the character, as sort of a doomy fate)<br /> <br /> Or maybe have Virtues and Vices as Paths. Someone who has a Virtue (Diligent) Path could have a job that pays well, has a fair amount of savings, and has friends who are also resourceful. That guy might also have the Vice (Vindictive) Path, and has a history of compiling dirt on people who offended him, hacking skills, and familiarity with police and the law... Just throwing around things at the dark here.<br /> <br /> Hmm, throwing idle thoughts back the WoD; a Garou character could have Breed-Auspice-Tribe Paths replacing Origin-Role-Society Paths respectively, have a Gnosis pool similar to a Talent's Inspiration pool, and shares a Rage pool with his packmates instead of the usual Momentum pool, and so on. Rank becomes something like Tiers, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:45:43-07:00","id":1486733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486709-storypath-patch-for-cod-2e?p=1486725#post1486725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is Tension? I don't think I've heard of it...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Tension</b> is 'Storyguide-only (GM) Momentum' - it raises by players spending their general Momentum pool. GM can spend Tension for things like rerolling 'bad' rolls for antagonists, making NPCs suddenly much more harder, saving major NPCs, activating truly powerfull powers of them, action interaption by villian in players turns, etc. GM get's points on start of story and it's much harder to get them later on for they.<br /> <br /> <i>'In addition to Base Tension, points are added to the Tension Pool whenever a player character overcomes a Condition or suffers a Failure Deed. This keeps the pool topped up according to the relative drama of the session.' </i>- <b>Scion Origin</b> p. 153<br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd</b>'s general comment - Getting (roll) Failure or Conditions are main sources for generating Momentum on players side.<br /> <br /> It's from earlier Storypath design, when engine was called <b>Sardonyx</b>. You get, <b>Sardonyx</b> as Momentum and Tension was in it, two forces, two colors. \ud83d\ude0e Tension is in <b>Scion</b> 2E, but NOT in <b>Trinity</b> or <b>They Came From</b> games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-17-2022, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T03:14:52-07:00","id":1486749,"title":"","content":"Ah, so it's in Scion. Haven't really kept up with that one.<br /> <br /> Yeah, reintroducing Tension looks like a good idea should Storypath ever be used to run CofD, at least on a glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T19:22:58-07:00","id":1487533,"title":"","content":"To be Storypath's biggest problem is the use of Scale. I just can't get my head around it? Like how do you determine what the scale of anything is? Is there a guide?<br /> <br /> I love alot of what it does like Atmosphere, and the Clue mechanics. But this is a big hurdle. Like if there was a way to use dervied stats to determine scale between things I think it would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 07-22-2022, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T20:05:12-07:00","id":1487536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486709-storypath-patch-for-cod-2e?p=1487533#post1487533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be Storypath's biggest problem is the use of Scale. I just can't get my head around it? Like how do you determine what the scale of anything is? Is there a guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Scales examples in various lines. From other experianced SGCs I hear that 'Scale is exponential'. So from Size Scale 0 to 1 ( <b>Scion</b> ), you go from human to car or truck size. For example, in <b>CoD</b>, even Gauru form of Uratha ( werewolves ), that is almost 3 meters high, is not enough to give Size Scale 1! \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> Directly about Size Scale it was in <b>Trinity Aberrant</b> corebook ( and KS preview I got ) and now in <b>Demigod </b>for <b>Scion</b>. Quoting the <b>Scion</b> table:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479645-sc-2e-demigod-scale-revisited-extended#post1479645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scale 0 \u2013 Baseline</b></span><br /> <b>Durability</b> \u2013 Basic clothing<br /> <b>Leadership</b> \u2013 Your neighbor<br /> <b>Mental</b> \u2013 Normal person<br /> <b>Power</b> \u2013 Amateur athlete<br /> <b>Might</b> \u2013 Knife or handgun<br /> <b>Size </b>\u2013 Person-sized<br /> <b>Speed</b> \u2013 Decent sprinter<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scale 1 \u2013 Elite</b></span><br /> <b>Durability </b>\u2013 Kevlar armor<br /> <b>Leadership</b> \u2013 Upper management<br /> <b>Mental</b> \u2013 Chess grandmaster<br /> <b>Power</b> \u2013 Gorilla<br /> <b>Might</b> \u2013 Anti-personnel riffle<br /> <b>Size</b> \u2013 Horse or Deer<br /> <b>Speed</b> \u2013 Cheetah, car<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scale 6 \u2013 Titanic</b></span><br /> <b>Durability </b>\u2013 Exotic matter not of this universe<br /> <b>Leadership</b> \u2013 Important God in the Pantheon<br /> <b>Mental</b> \u2013 Omniscient intellects<br /> <b>Power</b> \u2013 Moving of tectonic plate<br /> <b>Might</b> \u2013 Strategic thermonuclear device<br /> <b>Size</b> \u2013 Megalopolis<br /> <b>Speed</b> \u2013 Speed of Light<br /> [END of Table in book here]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}